[81.22, "o", "Three things to prioritize before this ships:\r\n\r\n1. **`divide` must return `Option<f64>`** (or `Result`) \u2014 returning `0.0` on division by zero is the most dangerous issue because it's *silent*. Callers have no way to detect the error, and the value can propagate into further calculations.\r\n\r\n2. **`fibonacci` needs `checked_add`** \u2014 the overflow only manifests in `--release`, which is exactly when you want correct behavior. `fibonacci(94)` silently returns a wrong answer today.\r\n\r\n3. **Add tests for `divide` and `word_count`** \u2014 two thirds of the public API is completely untested. The five test cases in the suggestions section above cover the minimum viable surface.\r\n"]
[81.2201, "o", "\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[>4m\u001b[<u\u001b[?1004l\u001b[?2031l\u001b[?2004l\u001b[?25h\u001b]9;4;0;\u0007"]
